ntrol, a fundamental opening principle\n- Prepares further development\n\nReason: d2-d4 is the strongest move because it completes the ideal central pawn duo, opens lines for piece development (especially the light-squared bishop on c1), and maintains White\'s initiative. This creates maximum central control and flexibility for further plans. It follows classical opening principles: control the center with pawns, then develop pieces.\n\nAnswer: P: d2-d4'}
