ith R: e1-b1 is the most forcing move available. The Black queen on b2 is my biggest immediate problem - it's deep in my position and controlling key squares. By attacking it directly, I force Black to move it, gaining a tempo. This also activates my rook along the b-file and may create counterplay opportunities. While my position is objectively losing due to material deficit, making forcing moves that create threats is the best practical try.\n\nAnswer: R: e1-b1"}
